  "narrative": "All new estimates are already signed to the registered direction. For main effects with direction -1, a positive signed estimate means PTEN-loss cells have stronger dependency_composite than PTEN-intact cells. For direction +1, positive means weaker dependency. For interactions, positive means the registered interaction direction is present. H124 tests PTEN loss among MSI-high-negative cells. It gives +0.2345 (95% +0.1382 to +0.3308; R131). The point estimate exceeds the 0.15-unit threshold and the sign is correct, but the lower bound remains just below threshold. Because this is the most direct remaining test of whether PTEN relevance survives removal of the very strong MSI-high predictor, I keep it unresolved and request independent validation rather than accept it. H133 tests PTEN loss among MSI-negative and low-mutation-burden cells and gives +0.2514 (+0.1211 to +0.3817; R132). It is concordant but less precise and also below threshold at the lower bound, so it supports the general PTEN context story but does not establish a threshold-sized effect; it is deferred. H125 tests whether PTEN-loss effects are amplified by high aneuploidy and gives -0.0029 (-0.1944 to +0.1886; R133). There is no evidence of the claimed interaction, so it is rejected and closed. H126 is invalid because one required cell has n=0, so the registered MYC-amplification-by-8q24 interaction cannot be evaluated as specified; I close it as unresolved rather than treating the invalid test as evidence against MYC biology. Technical moderators: H127, H128, and H129 test claimed amplification of core predictors in high-Cas9 cells. H127 gives -0.1701 (-0.3172 to -0.0230), which is opposite the claimed direction for SMARCA4-loss interaction. This is evidence of attenuation under high Cas9 activity rather than claimed amplification; I reject the registered H127 claim and do not promote the opposite direction to acceptance because it is post-hoc, multiple-tested, and a reversed interval would have lower bound only about +0.023. H128 gives -0.1427 (-0.2834 to -0.0021), again opposite the claimed direction and below threshold; reject and close. H129 gives -0.1155 (-0.3218 to +0.0908), null; reject and close. Adherent-growth moderators: H130 gives +0.0704 (-0.0718 to +0.2126), not supporting a threshold-sized SMARCA4 interaction; reject and close. H131 gives +0.1738 (+0.0180 to +0.3297), which is in the claimed KEAP1 direction and above threshold at the point estimate, but the lower bound is far below threshold and this is a post-hoc interaction screen; keep unresolved but deferred rather than accept. H132 gives +0.0392 (-0.1876 to +0.2660), null; reject and close. Overall, these new results do not establish a broad threshold-sized PTEN effect. They strengthen concordance of PTEN associations in non-MSI and low-TMB backgrounds but keep the conclusion context-dependent because lower confidence bounds remain below threshold. The core dataset-specific map remains: SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss with much weaker dependency; MSI-high with much stronger dependency; PTEN loss is a secondary context-specific association. The requested validation is H124 because it directly asks whether non-MSI PTEN loss can achieve an independent lower bound above 0.15. If validation succeeds, PTEN may be accepted in a broader non-MSI setting; if it fails, PTEN should remain restricted to already supported contexts.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific supported map: SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency_composite; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss with much weaker dependency_composite; MSI-high with much stronger dependency_composite. PTEN loss is a secondary context-specific association in several low-mask or non-MSI/low-TMB backgrounds, but broad PTEN remains unresolved because lower bounds repeatedly fall at or below 0.15, including after H111 validation failed. Iteration 11 new PTEN non-MSI tests: H124 +0.2345 lower +0.1382 (non-MSI PTEN, near threshold but not robust); H133 +0.2514 lower +0.1211 (non-MSI low-TMB, suggestive, deferred). H125 PTEN-by-aneuploidy interaction null/opposite, rejected. H126 MYC-by-8q24 interaction invalid due zero cell, closed unresolved. Technical Cas9 interactions: H127 SMARCA4 claimed direction rejected and showed opposite attenuation (-0.170 signed, raw opposite); H128 KEAP1 claimed direction opposite but subthreshold; H129 TP53 null. Adherent-growth interactions: H130 SMARCA4 null; H131 KEAP1 +0.174 lower +0.018, suggestive but not threshold robust, deferred; H132 TP53 null. Requested validation: H124, the most promising direct test of broader non-MSI PTEN. Proposed H134 as refinement: PTEN loss in non-MSI, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact cells. If H124 validates with lower bound >0.15, consider accepting broader non-MSI PTEN; otherwise keep PTEN context-specific and do not accept broad H32/H111. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable rules.",
